---
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../lib/site.ts";
---

<section class="section" id="licence">
  <div class="container licence-grid">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Licence</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Generator and dataset licences</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="licence-cards">
      <article class="card licence-card">
        <h3 class="h3">Generator: Apache-2.0</h3>
        <p class="body-text">
          The CLI, adapters, schemas, and Implementation Guide sources are Apache-2.0. We strictly
          separate that code from the medication catalog data and do not relicense the catalog.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card licence-card">
        <h3 class="h3">Datasets: upstream terms</h3>
        <p class="body-text">
          Catalog data keeps each provider’s own terms. Download cards show the flags below and a
          Terms link to the upstream page. Official builds checksum that page and halt redistribution
          if it no longer matches the reviewed snapshot.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <article class="card licence-card licence-flags-card">
      <h3 class="h3">What the flags mean</h3>
      <p class="body-text">
        <code class="mono">commercialUse</code>, <code class="mono">redistribution</code>, and
        <code class="mono">attributionRequired</code> on each artifact are
        <strong>indicators of our interpretation</strong> of the linked upstream terms at the dated
        review. They are not a licence grant and not legal advice.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Value</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">allowed</td>
            <td>We found an explicit grant for that activity in the linked terms.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">disallowed</td>
            <td>We found an explicit prohibition. The source is not in a public recipe.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">review-required</td>
            <td>Terms are missing, gated, or ambiguous. Not in a public recipe until resolved.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="body-text">
        <code class="mono">attributionRequired</code> is <code class="mono">true</code> or
        <code class="mono">false</code> according to whether those terms ask for attribution.
      </p>
      <p class="body-text">
        We are not liable for misinterpreting upstream licences. We are not liable for fitness for a
        specific purpose, or for legal compatibility or suitability for integration into any
        downstream product. Every customer bears the responsibility of cross-checking the linked
        upstream terms before use. We are not in control of how those terms are worded or when they
        change. The checksum in a release is a snapshot, not a guarantee the live page stays still.
      </p>
    </article>

    <p class="body-text">
      Source table:
      <a class="inline-link" href="/licence">Licence notes</a>. Tagging rubric:
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/docs/licences.md`}>docs/licences.md</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .licence-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .licence-grid .section-header {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .licence-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .licence-card {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.3rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .licence-flags-card table {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 720px) {
    .licence-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
